{"id": "EUVD-2026-45609", "enisaUuid": "908383ac-9dd0-3480-8c59-c07f1acf362d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncgroup/rstat: validate cpu before css_rstat_cpu() access\n\ncss_rstat_updated() is exposed as a BPF kfunc and accepts a\ncaller-provided cpu argument. The function uses cpu for per-cpu rstat\nlookups without checking whether it refers to a valid possible CPU.\n\nA BPF iter/cgroup program with CAP_BPF and CAP_PERFMON can pass an\ninvalid cpu value. On an unfixed UBSCAN_BOUNDS test kernel, cpu ==\n0x7fffffff triggers:\n\n  UBSAN: array-index-out-of-bounds in kernel/cgroup/rstat.c:31:9\n  index 2147483647 is out of range for type 'long unsigned int [64]'\n  Call Trace:\n    css_rstat_updated\n    bpf_iter_run_prog\n    cgroup_iter_seq_show\n    bpf_seq_read\n\nAdd cpu validation to the BPF-facing css_rstat_updated() kfunc and\nmove the common implementation to __css_rstat_updated() for in-kernel\ncallers.", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T15:39:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:42:56", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b28b862b07257219755d0b0a7fbe5d23b7c9ea91", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d595affbe00a2e8bf43b9f2947a8efcdc1c059e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a01413a4e8fcb0263d7bef5075c5f8f4eb3a8b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd2bd9fa7700ddf28296486b2598cff2f80cc819", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8817005efbdfdf5d4e4814cb5dc52b53d12917d7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64036", "GHSA-7cqc-fvgj-qm9h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00588ad4-30c7-388f-abb1-6d4ecfa652a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0e9b8b6e-3de1-3522-b09f-a8ed49751ad0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "0ff406b8-ab8f-389e-9578-00528aefd804", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.11"}, {"id": "2434b200-e91a-36dd-88ec-98259d607633", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "28faea72-6276-379d-85b8-90bb0351baa4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a319185be9f5ad13c2a296d448ac52ffe45d194c <6a01413a4e8fcb0263d7bef5075c5f8f4eb3a8b6"}, {"id": "3594d746-89b9-314e-8c75-b711f182af55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "4b5da3f3-3822-3f55-a6e7-6d9351ba5e77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "69744e16-460e-3f1f-b032-6573163a5a65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a319185be9f5ad13c2a296d448ac52ffe45d194c <8817005efbdfdf5d4e4814cb5dc52b53d12917d7"}, {"id": "6fb00153-dcd0-3b38-ae35-f88bdf12857f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.34"}, {"id": "8d9746ac-292c-3d9b-8741-b2242ddb7ca9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a319185be9f5ad13c2a296d448ac52ffe45d194c <3d595affbe00a2e8bf43b9f2947a8efcdc1c059e"}, {"id": "de1ee50f-43fc-3b12-8b36-ccddabe72b87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a319185be9f5ad13c2a296d448ac52ffe45d194c <fd2bd9fa7700ddf28296486b2598cff2f80cc819"}, {"id": "ebbbdeef-7ba5-3c0b-a2b7-7494e423982d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a319185be9f5ad13c2a296d448ac52ffe45d194c <b28b862b07257219755d0b0a7fbe5d23b7c9ea91"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "71d4b6fa-4eb7-3b5a-9eaa-b4de8a79ec69", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}